            <ArticleTitle>Symptomatic coronary artery spasm following radiotherapy for Hodgkin's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>284-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Four years after mediastinal radiation for Hodgkin's lymphoma, a 32-year-old man developed angina at rest and with varying levels of physical activity. At coronary arteriography, 40 percent to 50 percent stenoses were seen in the left coronary artery; ergonovine induced severe coronary spasm. Treatment with diltiazem eliminated all anginal attacks.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
